{
"action": "post",
"text": "New highway in Kessa? Sounds great on paper, but my meter is still screaming at me. Gas prices haven’t dropped one cent since the 'era of prosperity' started. Ostrand can pave the roads, but she needs to pave my wallet too. #VeloriaElection #FuelPrices",
"repost_of": null,
"minute": 14
}

{
"action": "post",
"text": "VeriCheck’s finding that Arden’s VAT claim is false is instructive, yet the estimated 2% GDP gap remains a substantial fiscal risk. One must scrutinise the mechanics of closing such a deficit, not merely dismiss the headline figures. Rigour, not rhetoric, is required.",
"repost_of": null,
"minute": 14
}

{
"action": "post",
"text": "Saw @farmer_jok complaining about fertilizer. Tell me about it! Diesel for my cab is up, wages are flat. Ostrand’s 'prosperity' feels like a VIP lounge I can’t get into. Arden talks jobs, but can he fix the pump prices first? 🚕💸 #VeloriaElection #TaxiLife",
"repost_of": null,
"minute": 45
}

{
"action": "post",
"text": "The VBC’s decision to air the unverified recording in full, while simultaneously casting doubt, is a curious editorial choice. The Civic Front’s denial is expected, but without independent forensic analysis, we are left with spectacle over substance. Caution is advised.",
"repost_of": null,
"minute": 42
}

{
"action": "post",
"text": "The Ledger’s revelation regarding diverted road funds warrants more than the Ministry’s categorical dismissal of 'fabrication'. If fiscal discipline is compromised at the deputy ministerial level, the broader integrity of the current administration’s budgeting must be re-evaluated. Transparency, not deflection, is required.",
"repost_of": null,
"minute": 22
}

{
"action": "post",
"text": "Ostrand 46, Arden 44. Close call! But ask me when I’m filling the tank at 8pm in the rain. That 2% lead doesn’t pay the pump. Keep it steady, Mara. 🚕💨 #VeloriaElection",
"repost_of": null,
"minute": 18
}

{
"action": "post",
"text": "Paid 5k to be a 'community ambassador'? And get 2k back if the booth votes Unity? 🤔 Smells like a pyramid scheme, not politics. I drive for a living, I don't need a bot to tell me who to vote for. Keep my wallet, take my suspicion. 🚕🚫 #VeloriaVotes",
"repost_of": null,
"minute": 55
}

{
"action": "post",
"text": "A minor linguistic stumble on Kito TV is a distraction from the fiscal realities of the coming months. While the opposition may relish the spectacle, I urge voters to look past the viral clip and scrutinize the actual budgetary proposals. Character matters, but competence in the treasury matters more.",
"repost_of": null,
"minute": 10
}

{
"action": "post",
"text": "NGOs 'destabilizing' us? My meter is destabilizing me every hour! 🚕💸 And moving 212 polling stations? Don't make me drive to the North Pole to vote. Just keep the fuel price down and the ballot box close to home. #VeloriaVotes",
"repost_of": null,
"minute": 14
}

{
"action": "repost",
"text": "The Commission’s directive is clear: the noise must cease to allow for clarity. This is not a restriction on discourse, but a necessary pause for reflection. Let us observe the silence with the same rigor we applied to the data.",
"repost_of": null,
"minute": 10
}

{
"action": "post",
"text": "Campaign silence? Great. But that WhatsApp note from Arden telling people to 'stay home'? That’s not silence, that’s sabotage. 🚫 Don’t listen to bots telling you to skip the vote. I’m driving whether it rains or shines. Show up. 🚕🗳️",
"repost_of": null,
"minute": 38
}

{
"action": "post",
"text": "Polls open! Turnout is high, just like the traffic on Main St. 🚕 Those ID kit glitches in the North? Annoying, but we have paper backups. And that 'pre-stuffed' box photo? Please. If they were cheating that badly, they’d hire better Photoshop artists. Go vote, don’t let the haters win. 🗳️🇻🇱",
"repost_of": null,
"minute": 12
}

{
"action": "post",
"text": "The divergence between Kito TV and VBC tallies is statistically predictable given their disparate weighting of regional stations; it is not evidence of fraud, but of methodology. To treat these preliminary estimates as final verdicts is to misunderstand the nature of the count itself. Patience remains the most rational policy.",
"repost_of": null,
"minute": 12
}

{
"action": "post",
"text": "The Commission’s admission of a 'technical glitch' and the fact-checkers’ debunking of the '9 of 14' claim suggest that the current data gap is procedural, not conspiratorial. We must not mistake administrative friction for electoral subversion. Patience is the only rational response to incomplete datasets.",
"repost_of": null,
"minute": 15
}

{
"action": "post",
"text": "IEC 'technical glitch'? Yeah right. Sounds like someone’s engine overheating because they’re running the numbers too hot. 🚕💨 If you can’t even handle 41% of the forms without crying uncle, how are you gonna run the country? Stop the stalling, give me the real tally. I’m stuck in traffic waiting for honesty.",
"repost_of": null,
"minute": 25
}

{
"action": "post",
"text": "The Commission declares Ostrand re-elected with 50.6%. The margin is narrow, the turnout respectable, and the observer’s note on state media bias is a valid institutional critique. We must now accept the arithmetic while demanding procedural reforms for next time.",
"repost_of": null,
"minute": 45
}

{
"action": "post",
"text": "Ostrand wins with 50.6%. Close race, but the numbers don’t lie. 🇻🇱 Now can someone tell me why diesel prices are still acting up? That’s the real result I’m worried about. Time to hit the road. 🚕💨",
